  "details": "It's great that you can create backups from the Creator Companion UI. It takes up less space on my hard drive than zipping the entire unity project itself. But if I want to restore a backup, I have to manually go to the folder where the backup is created, unzip the file, and add that directory to the creator companion as a new project.\n\nIt would be great if this process could be incorporated into the UI of the creator companion, for people who don't already know how these backups work and for user accessibility. Having a button to restore a backup and a dropdown for which backup to restore may be a really nice feature to implement.\n\nAdditionally, you could then implement the following features:\n\n- You could have an option to create a new backup of your current project before restoring the old backup.\n\n- You could have an option to delete old backups.\n\nI just think this would be a good idea. Thank you for implementing a backup feature!",
